[; cx-stdlib/authz — the XAP trust model + the single PEP decision
   function (spec/02-working/stdlib_authz.md). Principals, capabilities,
   attenuating/time-bounded/revocable delegations, guardian grants behind an
   incapacity-typed [gate …], the signed+versioned incapacity-predicate
   library, and the decision function check/authorize: actor × capability ×
   slice × tenant × unrevoked × required-tier (× guardian-gate) → a [permit]
   or [deny] VALUE. authz is the DECISION layer; the bus is the single
   ENFORCEMENT point that calls check.

   COMPOSES the shipped modules and adds NO crypto, NO transport, NO session,
   and NO new caps-capability of its own (§0/§1/§5): signature/tier verify is
   cx-stdlib/crypto; the (principal, tenant) actor is cx-stdlib/session;
   persistence/attribution is cx-stdlib/journal + cx-stdlib/store. authz is
   NOT caps — caps gates machine effects (this code may open a socket); authz
   gates DELEGATED AUTHORITY (Dana authorized ops-agent-1 to refund). They
   AND-compose, never substitute. Its only effects are reads/writes of trust
   state, gated by store's existing capability model — so, like
   journal/session, authz adds NO effect_alignment entry (the in-memory store
   is capability-free, the hermetic posture).

   FOUR-CHANNEL MODEL (SAP §1, §2.4/§2.5): a decision is a present
   [permit]/[deny] VALUE (a [deny] carries cx-err:CXER4700 as DATA, it is NOT
   an [err]); check is TOTAL (always permit or deny). A genuine fault is [err]
   (malformed grant / bright-line violation / signature failure / unknown
   predicate / store fault). An absent (revoked/expired/never-issued)
   delegation is the absence channel () — NOT null, NOT a [deny]. null is
   NEVER produced.

   FAIL-CLOSED (§4): deny by default; any ambiguity denies. A guardian grant
   permits ONLY while its incapacity gate holds and ONLY its pinned [action …]
   — the instant the principal re-engages the gate goes false and check flips
   to [deny] with no explicit revoke (falsifiable-by-presence, §4.4).

   BRIGHT LINE as a TYPE CONSTRAINT (§4.4): a guardian [gate …] admits ONLY
   `incapacity` (signed-library name@version) + `state` (CXPath threshold)
   leaves over all/any/not. A leaf branching on a principal's CHOICE
   (declined/refused/consent/…) is rejected at AUTHORING → CXER4701. A gate
   needs ≥ 1 incapacity → else CXER4702. Inline/ad-hoc incapacity → CXER4706.

   ERROR BAND cx-err:CXER4700–4799 (§8): 4700 UNAUTHORIZED (the canonical
   authority-denied code; carried as data in every [deny], raised only under
   authorize raise-on-deny=true) / 4701 REFUSAL_TRIGGER / 4702 GATE_ILLFORMED
   / 4703 ESCALATION / 4704 VERIFY_FAILED / 4705 EXPIRED / 4706
   UNKNOWN_PREDICATE / 4707 REVOKED / 4708 TENANT_MISMATCH / 4709
   NO_RELATIONSHIP / 4710 STORE_FAULT / 4711 ARG_INVALID / 4712 HANDLE_CLOSED.
   Cancellation is the core CXER0260; caps denial the core CXER0271 (both
   inherited, never authz codes).

   The trailing $opts::map {} are DEFAULTED positional parameters
   (grammar.ebnf [153b]).

   NOTE: this const and the native primitives (vcx/code/stdlib_authz.v) are
   the same surface — edit both. ]

[; §3.1 authority store construction (the trust-state backend) ]
[?def store scope=public impure [returns element] ($opts::map {})    [$authz-store $opts]]
[?def close scope=public impure [returns null]    ($handle::element)  [$authz-close $handle]]

[; §3.2 issue + revoke a delegation (the dial) ]
[?def delegate scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $delegation::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-delegate $store $delegation $opts]]
[?def revoke   scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $id::string         $opts::map {}) [$authz-revoke $store $id $opts]]

[; §3.3 issue a guardian grant (the conditional pre-issued delegation) ]
[?def grant-guardian scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $grant::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-grant-guardian $store $grant $opts]]

[; §3.4 the PEP decision function — check / authorize (pure) ]
[?def check     scope=public pure [returns element]            ($store::element $req::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-check $store $req $opts]]
[?def authorize scope=public pure [returns element]            ($store::element $req::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-authorize $store $req $opts]]
[?def find      scope=public pure [returns element]            ($store::element $id::string)                 [$authz-find $store $id]]
[?def grants-of scope=public pure [returns [sequence element]] ($store::element $actor::element)             [$authz-grants-of $store $actor]]

[; §3.5 the incapacity-predicate library + gate well-formedness ]
[?def predicate        scope=public pure   [returns element]            ($store::element $name-at-version::string) [$authz-predicate $store $name-at-version]]
[?def predicates       scope=public pure   [returns [sequence element]] ($store::element)                          [$authz-predicates $store]]
[; gate-wellformed: the spec names this `gate-wellformed?`, but `?` is not a
   grammar NameChar in a call head ([$authz:VERB …]) — the same constraint that
   forced net's addr->string → addr-to-string. The verb is spelled WITHOUT the
   trailing `?`; semantics are identical (a [valid]/[invalid] VALUE, never an
   [err]). ]
[?def gate-wellformed scope=public pure    [returns element]            ($gate::element $opts::map {})            [$authz-gate-wellformed $gate $opts]]
[?def verify-tier      scope=public impure [returns element]            ($store::element $grant::element $tier::string "" $opts::map {}) [$authz-verify-tier $store $grant $tier $opts]]

[; §3.6 effective envelope — the intersection (pure) ]
[?def effective scope=public pure [returns element] ($store::element $actor::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-effective $store $actor $opts]]

[; §3.7 dry-run / explain / trace — why can / can't X do Y? (pure) ]
[?def dry-run scope=public pure [returns element]            ($store::element $req::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-dry-run $store $req $opts]]
[?def explain scope=public pure [returns element]            ($decision::element)                          [$authz-explain $decision]]
[?def trace   scope=public pure [returns [sequence element]] ($store::element $req::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-trace $store $req $opts]]

[; §3.8 budgets (stream 6, L112) — meter-as-fold + the commit-point debit.
   meters folds the bound journal's debit events into the snapshot value
   check reads ({meters: …} — check stays pure); debit charges a meter at
   the commit point (journal append under the stream's commit lock),
   re-checking headroom under the lock (exhausted = the CXER4713-carrying
   [deny …] VALUE, no event). Both need the durable (journal-bound) tier. ]
[?def meters scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-meters $store $opts]]
[?def debit  scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $id::string $opts::map {}) [$authz-debit $store $id $opts]]
[?def allocate       scope=public impure [effects [write]] [returns element] ($store::element $alloc-id::string $opts::map) [$authz-allocate $store $alloc-id $opts]]
[?def allocation-expire scope=public impure [effects [write]] [returns element] ($store::element $alloc-id::string $opts::map {}) [$authz-allocation-expire $store $alloc-id $opts]]

[; §3.9 propose-mode disposition (stream 6, L113/L114) — the engine constructs
   proposals (cx:propose); authz disposes: approve mints the Lane-2 claim
   binding the proposal ADDRESS; commit verifies fail-closed (address binding,
   tier, propose-only screening, requires re-resolution, version binding,
   precondition re-check) then executes, debits, and journals; resolve-cap
   resolves a cap: authority-artifact address against the LIVE registry. ]
[?def approve     scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $proposal::element $opts::map {}) [$authz-approve $store $proposal $opts]]
[?def commit      scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $proposal::element $approval::element $command::function $opts::map {}) [$authz-commit $store $proposal $approval $command $opts]]
[?def resolve-cap scope=public impure [returns element] ($store::element $ref::string $opts::map {}) [$authz-resolve-cap $store $ref $opts]]

[; co-located docs (seeded — refine in place). ]
[module-doc name=authz
  [scope """The XAP authority model as data plus a single decision function. It represents principals, capabilities, attenuating/time-bounded/revocable delegations, and guardian grants gated behind incapacity-typed predicates, then decides authority at one point of enforcement: check/authorize answers whether an actor holds a capability over a slice in a tenant at the required assurance tier, returning a [permit] or [deny] value. Authority originates only from principals and can only attenuate down a delegation chain, so privilege escalation is structurally impossible. This is delegated authority — who authorized whom to do what — distinct from and AND-composed with the effect-permission capability system."""]]
[fn-doc name=store scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Open an authority store — the trust-state handle for one tenant, taken by the persisting and live-read verbs."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund-duplicate]] [over '/orders'] [assurance :t1] [signature sig-dana]]]]
  [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent ops-1]] [capability refund-duplicate] [slice '/orders/9'] [tenant acme]]]]"""] [expect """[permit rooted-principal=dana [delegation 'd-1'] [via 'd-1'] [tier :t1] [capability 'refund-duplicate']]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=close scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> null"""]
  [summary """Close an authority store — idempotent, never raises."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $c [$authz:close $az]]
  [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent x]] [capability y] [tenant acme]]]]"""] [expect """cx-err:CXER4712"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=delegate scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Issue an ordinary delegation, enforcing attenuation — conveying more than the issuer holds raises CXER4703."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund-duplicate]] [over '/orders'] [assurance :t1] [signature sig-dana]]]]
  [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent ops-1]] [capability refund-duplicate] [slice '/orders/9'] [tenant acme]]]]"""] [expect """[permit rooted-principal=dana [delegation 'd-1'] [via 'd-1'] [tier :t1] [capability 'refund-duplicate']]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=revoke scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Revoke a delegation by id — idempotent; opts.cascade also revokes everything it sourced."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund]] [over '/orders'] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
  [= $r [$authz:revoke $az 'd-1']]
  [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent ops-1]] [capability refund] [slice '/orders/9'] [tenant acme]]]]"""] [expect """[deny actor=ops-1 [code 'cx-err:CXER4700'] [reason :no-grant] [capability 'refund'] [slice '/orders/9'] [tenant id=acme]]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=grant-guardian scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Issue a guardian grant after the full two-validator check, storing it dormant until its incapacity gate fires."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $g [$authz:grant-guardian $az
    [delegation g-1 [tenant acme] [mode :guardian] [from [principal admin]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [pause-gw]] [action [do :pause-gw]]
      [gate [all [incapacity [no-ack-within [of :escalation]]] [state [gt '/charge-error-rate' 0.15]]]]
      [assurance :t1] [signature sig-admin]]]]
  [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent ops-1]] [capability pause-gw] [tenant acme]]
    {with-context: [context [no-ack-within true] [charge-error-rate 0.2]]}]]"""] [expect """[permit rooted-principal=admin [delegation 'g-1'] [via 'g-1'] [tier :t1] [capability 'pause-gw']]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=check scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Decide an authorization request at the single PEP, returning a [permit] or [deny] value — always total."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund-duplicate]] [over '/orders'] [assurance :t1] [signature sig-dana]]]]
  [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent ops-1]] [capability refund-duplicate] [slice '/orders/9'] [tenant acme]]]]"""] [expect """[permit rooted-principal=dana [delegation 'd-1'] [via 'd-1'] [tier :t1] [capability 'refund-duplicate']]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=authorize scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """The strict alias of check — with raise-on-deny=true a [deny] becomes a raised CXER4700."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [$authz:authorize $az [authz-request [actor [agent x]] [capability y] [tenant acme]] {raise-on-deny: true}]]"""] [expect """cx-err:CXER4700"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=find scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Look up a delegation by id — never-issued, revoked, or expired yields the absence channel."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund]] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
  [$authz:find $az 'd-1']]"""] [expect """[delegation id=d-1 mode=delegated state=active [tenant id=acme] [to [agent id=ops-1]] [from [principal id=dana]] [capabilities [refund]] [assurance :t1]]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=grants-of scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> [sequence element]"""]
  [summary """List all currently-active delegations granted to an actor, in receive order."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund]] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
  [$authz:grants-of $az [agent ops-1]]]"""] [expect """([delegation id=d-1 mode=delegated state=active [tenant id=acme] [to [agent id=ops-1]] [from [principal id=dana]] [capabilities [refund]] [assurance :t1]])"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=predicate scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Look up a signed-library incapacity predicate by name@version — unknown yields the absence channel."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [$authz:predicate $az 'no-ack-within@v1']]"""] [expect """[predicate name=no-ack-within version=v1 [params [duration] [of]] [rationale 'a request was issued and no acknowledgement arrived within the window — truth depends on the elapsed clock + the absence of an ack event, never on the principal willing it; an ack the instant it arrives makes it false'] [signature 'bundled-library:no-ack-within@v1']]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=predicates scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> [sequence element]"""]
  [summary """List the whole signed incapacity-predicate library."""]
]
[fn-doc name=gate-wellformed scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Run the structural and semantic validators over a [gate …] without issuing, returning a [valid] or [invalid …] value."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[$authz:gate-wellformed [gate [all [incapacity [no-ack-within]] [state [gt '/x' 1]]]]]"""] [expect """[valid]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=verify-tier scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Verify a grant's assurance tier via crypto — returns [verified …] or raises CXER4704."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [$authz:verify-tier $az
    [delegation d [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent o]]
      [capabilities [x]] [assurance :t1] [signature sig-ok]] 't1']]"""] [expect """[verified [tier :t1]]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=effective scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Compute an actor's effective envelope — the most-restrictive intersection of individual and superior/managing/collective gates."""]
]
[fn-doc name=dry-run scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Run check over an explicit scenario with no journal write, returning the same [permit] or [deny] value."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent o]]
      [capabilities [x]] [over '/s'] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
  [$authz:dry-run $az [authz-request [actor [agent o]] [capability x] [slice '/s/1'] [tenant acme]]]]"""] [expect """[permit rooted-principal=dana [delegation 'd'] [via 'd'] [tier :t1] [capability 'x']]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=explain scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Turn a permit or deny into a readable [explanation …] — the authority chain or the first failing link."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let [= $az [$authz:store {tenant: 'acme'}]]
  [= $d [$authz:delegate $az
    [delegation d-1 [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent ops-1]]
      [capabilities [refund]] [over '/orders'] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
  [= $dec [$authz:check $az [authz-request [actor [agent ops-1]] [capability refund] [slice '/orders/9'] [tenant acme]]]]
  [$authz:explain $dec]]"""] [expect """[explanation outcome=permit [accountable 'dana'] [authority-chain [step 'd-1']]]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=trace scope=public purity=pure
  [sig """-> [sequence element]"""]
  [summary """Return the ordered policy-stack evaluation behind a decision — the deep-debug view behind explain."""]
]

[fn-doc name=meters scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Fold the bound journal's debit events into the [meters ...] snapshot check reads ({meters: ...}) — rate as token-bucket replay, count monotone, spend inside the current UTC-Z window; opts.now pins the fold instant. Needs the journal-bound (durable) tier."""]
]

[fn-doc name=debit scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Charge a delegation's meters at the commit point: re-checks headroom under the journal stream's commit lock, appends the authz-debited event, and returns a [debited ...] receipt — exhausted yields the CXER4713-carrying [deny ...] value and writes nothing. Refunds never credit back."""]
]
[fn-doc name=allocate scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Reserve an ESCROW ALLOCATION from a parent delegation's meter (stream 10, cross_stream_coordination §3): the reservation debits the parent chain AT ALLOCATION TIME under the parent's commit lock (an uncoverable reservation is the CXER4713 deny naming the failing conjunct — the global cap enforces here, never at a later cross-stream draw); window attribution pins at the reservation instant. Scope: count and spend ONLY — rate is a flow property (a reserved rate is unused capacity or double-counted flow) and refuses; a sub-delegation carrying rate meters it locally, un-escrowed. Allocation ids are single-use (reserve once, draw via debit {allocation: id}, expire)."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let
[= $s [$store:open "mem://esc-1"]]
[= $j [$journal:attach $s "acme"]]
[= $az [$authz:store {tenant: "acme" journal: $j}]]
[= $d [$authz:delegate $az
  [delegation d-parent [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent team-1]]
    [capabilities [spend-money]] [bounds [count 10] [spend 100.0 :currency :USD :per '1d']] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
[= $a1 [$authz:allocate $az "esc-1" {from: "d-parent" count: 4 spend: 40.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T10:00:00Z"}]]
[= $rate-refused [?fallback [$authz:allocate $az "esc-r" {from: "d-parent" rate: {n: 5 per: "PT1M"}}] [recover-with [context] [code $err@code]]]]
[= $over [$authz:allocate $az "esc-2" {from: "d-parent" spend: 70.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T10:01:00Z"}]]
[= $draw1 [$authz:debit $az "d-parent" {allocation: "esc-1" count: 2 spend: 15.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T10:05:00Z"}]]
[= $draw-over [$authz:debit $az "d-parent" {allocation: "esc-1" count: 3 at: "2026-08-12T10:06:00Z"}]]
[= $exp [$authz:allocation-expire $az "esc-1" {at: "2026-08-12T11:00:00Z"}]]
[= $draw-late [$authz:debit $az "d-parent" {allocation: "esc-1" count: 1 at: "2026-08-12T11:05:00Z"}]]
[= $after [$authz:allocate $az "esc-3" {from: "d-parent" spend: 70.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T11:10:00Z"}]]
  [probe [reserved $a1] [rate $rate-refused] [over-reserve $over] [draw $draw1] [draw-over $draw-over] [expired $exp] [draw-late $draw-late] [reclaimed-then-ok $after]]]"""] [expect """[probe [reserved [allocated alloc=esc-1 from=d-parent count=4 spend=4.0e1 currency=USD]] [rate [code 'cx-err:CXER4711']] [over-reserve [deny [code 'cx-err:CXER4713'] [reason :budget-exhausted] [conjunct :spend] [delegation 'd-parent']]] [draw [debited id=d-parent alloc=esc-1 count=2 spend=1.5e1 currency=USD]] [draw-over [deny [code 'cx-err:CXER4713'] [reason :budget-exhausted] [conjunct :allocation-count] [delegation 'esc-1']]] [expired [allocation-expired alloc=esc-1 reclaimed-count=2 reclaimed-spend=2.5e1]] [draw-late [deny [code 'cx-err:CXER4713'] [reason :budget-exhausted] [conjunct :allocation-expired] [delegation 'esc-1']]] [reclaimed-then-ok [allocated alloc=esc-3 from=d-parent spend=7.0e1 currency=USD]]]"""]]
]
[fn-doc name=allocation-expire scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Expire an allocation, reclaiming its UN-DRAWN remainder — visibly (reclaimed-count/reclaimed-spend) and WITHOUT replenishment: the un-drawn part never left the window's budget, so reclaiming it restores availability while spent budget stays monotone (the two rules compose). After expiry the parent's consumption for the allocation is exactly what was drawn; further draws against it deny naming :allocation-expired. Typically armed via a sched durable timer."""]
  [example [code """[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/journal']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/authz']
[?let
[= $s [$store:open "mem://esc-1"]]
[= $j [$journal:attach $s "acme"]]
[= $az [$authz:store {tenant: "acme" journal: $j}]]
[= $d [$authz:delegate $az
  [delegation d-parent [tenant acme] [from [principal dana]] [to [agent team-1]]
    [capabilities [spend-money]] [bounds [count 10] [spend 100.0 :currency :USD :per '1d']] [assurance :t1] [signature s]]]]
[= $a1 [$authz:allocate $az "esc-1" {from: "d-parent" count: 4 spend: 40.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T10:00:00Z"}]]
[= $rate-refused [?fallback [$authz:allocate $az "esc-r" {from: "d-parent" rate: {n: 5 per: "PT1M"}}] [recover-with [context] [code $err@code]]]]
[= $over [$authz:allocate $az "esc-2" {from: "d-parent" spend: 70.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T10:01:00Z"}]]
[= $draw1 [$authz:debit $az "d-parent" {allocation: "esc-1" count: 2 spend: 15.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T10:05:00Z"}]]
[= $draw-over [$authz:debit $az "d-parent" {allocation: "esc-1" count: 3 at: "2026-08-12T10:06:00Z"}]]
[= $exp [$authz:allocation-expire $az "esc-1" {at: "2026-08-12T11:00:00Z"}]]
[= $draw-late [$authz:debit $az "d-parent" {allocation: "esc-1" count: 1 at: "2026-08-12T11:05:00Z"}]]
[= $after [$authz:allocate $az "esc-3" {from: "d-parent" spend: 70.0 currency: "USD" at: "2026-08-12T11:10:00Z"}]]
  [probe [reserved $a1] [rate $rate-refused] [over-reserve $over] [draw $draw1] [draw-over $draw-over] [expired $exp] [draw-late $draw-late] [reclaimed-then-ok $after]]]"""] [expect """[probe [reserved [allocated alloc=esc-1 from=d-parent count=4 spend=4.0e1 currency=USD]] [rate [code 'cx-err:CXER4711']] [over-reserve [deny [code 'cx-err:CXER4713'] [reason :budget-exhausted] [conjunct :spend] [delegation 'd-parent']]] [draw [debited id=d-parent alloc=esc-1 count=2 spend=1.5e1 currency=USD]] [draw-over [deny [code 'cx-err:CXER4713'] [reason :budget-exhausted] [conjunct :allocation-count] [delegation 'esc-1']]] [expired [allocation-expired alloc=esc-1 reclaimed-count=2 reclaimed-spend=2.5e1]] [draw-late [deny [code 'cx-err:CXER4713'] [reason :budget-exhausted] [conjunct :allocation-expired] [delegation 'esc-1']]] [reclaimed-then-ok [allocated alloc=esc-3 from=d-parent spend=7.0e1 currency=USD]]]"""]]
]

[fn-doc name=approve scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Mint the [approval ...] claim binding a proposal's Tier-1 ADDRESS (never a name or args — forgeable): opts.by names the principal, opts.tier the assurance tier, opts.signature the suite slot (mandatory; verifiers fail closed)."""]
]

[fn-doc name=commit scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Dispose an approved proposal fail-closed: the proposal must re-hash to the approval's subject, the approval must verify per its tier, no propose-only link may ground the basis, requires cap: refs re-resolve, the presented command must match the approved def-text address, preconditions re-evaluate — then execute, debit under the commit lock, and journal the transition. Needs the journal-bound tier."""]
]

[fn-doc name=resolve-cap scope=public purity=impure
  [sig """-> element"""]
  [summary """Resolve a cap:sha2-256 authority-artifact address against the LIVE registry view — the artifact must exist, be un-revoked, and un-expired; anything else is the fail-closed CXER4716 (a trust input that cannot be proven live is refused)."""]
]
